<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<RecordType xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        RecordType.Description is capped at 255 characters. The full rationale below is
        operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API. Do not paste this back into
        <description>. NOTE ALSO: the comment must sit INSIDE the root element - a comment
        placed ABOVE <RecordType> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        THE BROKER-LISTED DISPOSITION PATH. ELEVEN STAGES:
        Disposition Readiness, BOV Outreach, Broker Selection, NDA, Release Materials,
        Active Listing, Offer Selection, LOI, PSA, Closing, Sale Closes.

        THIS IS THE DEFAULT TYPE. DispositionService stamps it EXPLICITLY when the Sell Meter
        creates a disposition, rather than leaving RecordTypeId null and inheriting the running
        user's PROFILE default - profiles are .forceignore'd, so that default is org state this
        repo cannot see, set or verify. From 2026-08-19 the Initiate modal makes the choice an
        explicit, MANDATORY radio at creation time instead of a later switch.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 RETRACTED 2026-08-19 - THE OFF-MARKET-ONLY DOCTRINE THIS FILE CARRIED IS DEAD.
        =====================================================================================
        The superseded paragraph is quoted and retracted rather than deleted, because it is an
        instruction that told the next reader NOT to make the exact change this redesign makes:

            RETRACTED: "Disposition_Stage__c is restricted here to the EIGHT on-market stages.
            NDA and Disposition Offer are off-market stage values ONLY and are deliberately
            excluded - the source document narrates a buyer NDA and an offer inside the
            on-market path too, but as RECORDS surfaced during other stages, not as stages. Do
            not 'helpfully' add them here."

        WHAT REPLACED IT: THE CLIENT REDEFINED THE FLOW. NDA IS NOW A STAGE ON BOTH PATHS - an
        on-market deal collects NDAs from interested parties before materials are released,
        exactly as an off-market one does, and the all-NDAs-signed gate now applies to both
        (All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression dropped its record-type term in the same change).
        Broker Selection, Release Materials, Offer Selection and Sale Closes are likewise on
        BOTH types. NINE of the eleven values here are shared with Off_Market.

        🔴 THE CONSEQUENCE THAT MATTERS MOST: THE STAGE VALUE NO LONGER IDENTIFIES THE PATH.
        Only BOV Outreach and Active Listing are on-market-only now, and only Disposition Offer
        (retired) was ever off-market-only. Any component that needs to know which path a record
        is on must test the RECORD TYPE. That is what Disposition__c.Is_On_Market__c exists for;
        lwc/dispositionSidebar's "the two value sets are DISJOINT" comment was retracted in the
        same change.

        =====================================================================================
        THE TRANSITION-WINDOW UNION - WHY THIS LIST HAD 13 VALUES AND NOT 11 (2026-08-19 TO
        2026-08-21).
        =====================================================================================
        Call for Offers and Completed were RETIRED but stayed listed for the transition window.
        A metadata deploy CANNOT delete a picklist value, so they stayed on Disposition_Stage__c
        until the manual Setup deletion wave removed them; and a record type cannot reference a
        value that no longer exists, so they had to stay listed here until that wave ran.
        Disposition Offer was never on this type and this change never added it.

        🔴 RETIRED 2026-08-21 (offer-form-and-stage-retirement.md, Request C). Both values are
        now removed below, in the SAME commit as Disposition_Stage__c.field-meta.xml,
        Off_Market.recordType-meta.xml and the objectTranslations file - splitting them fails,
        because this file would then reference a value the field no longer declares. This edit
        must NOT be deployed until the manual Setup deletion of both values (and Completed's
        deletion for Off_Market) has already happened; deploying first is a silent no-op that a
        later retrieve then undoes by re-adding them.

        Sell_Decision_Trigger__c is enumerated in full because a record type file must list
        EVERY picklist on the object or values are silently dropped from that type.
        Disposition__c has exactly two picklists today.

        No <businessProcess> - that element is for Opportunity, Case, Lead and Solution only.

        ⚠ RECORD-TYPE PICKLIST RESTRICTION IS UI-ONLY. An API, seed or data-load write can put
        an off-market value on an on-market row. The gates that MATTER are the validation rules
        and the server-side asserts in DispositionApprovalService, not this list.
    -->
    <fullName>On_Market</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>The broker-listed path, 11 stages: Readiness, BOV Outreach, Broker Selection, NDA, Release Materials, Active Listing, Offer Selection, LOI, PSA, Closing, Sale Closes. Default type. Call for Offers and Completed retired 2026-08-21.</description>
    <label>On Market</label>
